<p>Decimal 36869. Raw name for this VIC chip register. Also known as <strong>VIC_DATA_LOC</strong>, where the full description lives.</p>
<p>Screen map and character set addresses.</p>
<ul>
<li>Bits 7-4 - screen address bits 13-10 (see table)</li>
<li>Bits 3-0 - character set address bits 13-10 (see table)</li>
</ul>

<p>Screen address - bits 7-4, VICCR2 bit 7<br />
$1000 = 1100, 0<br />
$1200 = 1100, 1<br />
$1400 = 1101, 0<br />
$1600 = 1101, 1<br />
$1800 = 1110, 0<br />
$1A00 = 1110, 1<br />
$1C00 = 1111, 0<br />
$1E00 = 1111, 1<br />
</p>

<p>Character set address - bits 3-0<br />
$8000 = 0000 (ROM character set)<br />
$8400 = 0001<br />
$8800 = 0010 (ROM upper case and graphics)<br />
$8C00 = 0011<br />
$9000 = 0100<br />
$9400 = 0101<br />
$9800 = 0110<br />
$9C00 = 0111<br />
$0000 = 1000 (RAM from here down)<br />
$0400 = 1001<br />
$0800 = 1010<br />
$0C00 = 1011<br />
$1000 = 1100<br />
$1400 = 1101<br />
$1800 = 1110<br />
$1C00 = 1111<br />
</p>
